---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HubPageShell from '../components/hub/HubPageShell.astro';
import '../styles/redesign.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Investigate Further in Arizona"
  description="Optional next steps after education for Arizona homeowners considering a second opinion or independent floor survey."
  hub={true}
>
  <HubPageShell
    title="Investigate Further in Arizona"
    subhead="Education first. Next steps only if you choose them."
    bannerBlurb="MFRC is an educational resource. It does not inspect houses or sell repair. If you want a measured second look in Arizona, one option is listed below."
    glance={[
      { label: 'This page', value: 'Optional next step' },
      { label: 'MFRC', value: 'Education only' },
      { label: 'Arizona option', value: 'Independent second opinion' },
      { label: 'Not required', value: 'Many concerns stay at learning' },
    ]}
    nav={[]}
    topicsStyle="list"
  >
    <div class="intro">
      <p>MFRC is an educational website created to help homeowners understand common foundation topics before deciding whether any further action is needed.</p>
      <p>This site does not provide inspections, evaluations, or repair recommendations. Many foundation concerns never progress beyond learning, monitoring, and asking better questions.</p>
      <p>If you choose to explore a next step in Arizona beyond education, the option below may be appropriate.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-heading">Independent second opinion and floor survey</h2>
    <div class="content-block">
      <p>Some Arizona homeowners already have a repair estimate and want an independent read of the house before they sign. Others want a measured floor survey that is not tied to selling piers.</p>
      <p>Foundation Repair Advocate offers paid floor elevation surveys and second opinions for Arizona homeowners. It is not a free sales inspection and not a pier company.</p>
      <div class="related-links">
        <a href="https://www.foundationrepairadvocate.com" rel="noopener">Foundation Repair Advocate →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-block">
      <p>MFRC remains educational. The people who write this content also work in the field. That does not change the purpose of this site.</p>
    </div>
  </HubPageShell>
</BaseLayout>
